  "id": "COMPOUND:17232 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "Isoiguesterin is implicated in the regulation of Thrombopoietin through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Isoiguesterin acts as a target for multiple compounds, which in turn target H9, a protein that is itself a target of several other molecules. These pathways ultimately converge on Thrombopoietin, indicating a potential role in the modulation of thrombopoiesis. The presence of multiple distinct targets (H9, Daedaleasides A, 15,16-Epoxy-15Alpha-Methoxy-Ent-Clerod-3-En-18-Oic Acid, and Getiacaulein) suggests that Isoiguesterin may influence the expression or activity of these proteins, which in turn affect Thrombopoietin. The integration of these pathways highlights a complex network where Isoiguesterin could serve as a central node in the regulation of thrombopoietin, possibly through indirect mechanisms involving protein interactions and signaling pathways.",
